<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taj al-Din Harb</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1215">1215</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taj al-Din Harb ibn Muhammad was the Nasrid malik of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sistan</a> who ruled for nearly fifty years until his death in 1215. Ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaranj">Zaranj</a>, he kept his house in power by accepting the overlordship first of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> and then of the Ghurids, whose campaigns he supported with troops. His long reign was the high point of the dynasty before the Mongol invasion.</p></div>
